---
import DrawbridgeLayout from "@/layouts/DrawbridgeLayout.astro";
---

<DrawbridgeLayout title="Privacy" description="Drawbridge privacy details: nothing leaves your device.">
  <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-3xl gap-8">
    <div class="grid gap-2 text-center">
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground">Drawbridge is built so that nothing leaves your device.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid gap-6 text-foreground">
      <section class="grid gap-3">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">What we do not do</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          <li>No server-side processing.</li>
          <li>No analytics or tracking.</li>
          <li>No cookies.</li>
          <li>No account or login.</li>
          <li>No network requests after the page is loaded.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="grid gap-3">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">How it works</h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          Drawbridge is a static site. When you open a tool, the page and its code are served to your browser. Any file
          you import or text you paste is processed in memory by JavaScript running on your own device.
        </p>
        <p class="leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          The production site sends a Content Security Policy header that blocks external requests (
          <code>default-src 'self'</code>). This means even if malicious code were somehow introduced, it could not send
          your data to another server.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="grid gap-3">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Local preferences</h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          Drawbridge stores a few small preferences in your browser’s localStorage so your choices persist between
          visits. This currently includes your selected color theme and whether the quick-start guide is open on each
          tool page. These values never leave your device and are not transmitted anywhere.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="grid gap-3">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Offline use</h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          Drawbridge is an installable progressive web app. After the first load, a service worker caches the site so it
          works without a network connection. You can verify this by turning off Wi-Fi after the initial load.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="grid gap-3">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Recommendations for sensitive data</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          <li>Use a private or incognito browser window.</li>
          <li>Disable browser extensions you do not trust.</li>
          <li>Turn off your network connection after loading the site.</li>
          <li>Close the tab when you are finished.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</DrawbridgeLayout>
